      <Line>The conduction losses modelled in the third quadrant are obtained with</Line>
      <Line>the switch always on. Therefore, body-diode conduction during deadtime</Line>
      <Line>is not modelled!</Line>
      <Line>The Eon/Eoff energies are determined via double-pulse</Line>
      <Line>simulations in SIMetrix.For the switching losses, an SiC diode is used</Line>
      <Line>on the top side of the half bridge for CoolMOS, unless otherwise specified and an</Line>
      <Line>identical switch in the case of CoolSiC and CoolGaN.</Line>
      <Line>The body diode-like voltage drop for CoolGaN is measured at 0V Vgs.</Line>
      <Line>The double-pulse simulation contains a lumped</Line>
      <Line>parasitic inductance as indicated in the disclaimer.</Line>
      <Line>The energy values are obtained by electrical measurements of</Line>
      <Line>voltage and current according to Infineon internal criteria.</Line>
      <Line>Since electrical measurements overestimate the Eoff losses,</Line>
      <Line>we correct this behavior by transferring the Eoss-related</Line>
      <Line>energy to the respective turn-on energies.</Line>
      <Line></Line>
      <Line>Qrr is not modelled explicitly - it is implicitly included in the energy values.</Line>
      <Line></Line>
      <Line>The thermal network in the PLECS model is identical to the thermal</Line>
      <Line>network in the L3 SIMetrix model.</Line>
      <Line></Line>
      <Line>If higher accuracy is needed, we recommend performing</Line>
      <Line>additional SPICE simulations with our SIMetrix models!</Line>
      <Line>Please use the Infineon Developer Community</Line>
      <Line>(https://community.infineon.com) for further information and support!</Line>
      <Line></Line>
      <Line>The simulation results outside of the provided power loss data range may not be accurate.</Line>
      <Line>The upper side switch for the double pulse tests (commutation partner) is a IGLD65R055D2.</Line>
      <Line>Vds range is 0V to 500V.</Line>
      <Line>Id range is 0A to 20.0A.</Line>
      <Line>Tj range is 25C to 150C.</Line>
